 "engine_service_gaps_measured": {
  "E1": "/verts (legacy and C3 delta) carry no ts_us; the slice server pairs /verts with /tick_state; measured pairing gap median 0.8-0.9 ms, p95 ~21 ms (engine lock-starvation tail) -- the ambiguity is bounded and shipped in every snapshot header",
  "E2": "the engine serves a state read in ~15 ms median (single HTTP worker, min 0.65 ms => lock starvation, not work): one client's 60 Hz snapshot subscription costs 2 pulls and exceeds the budget; measured 60 Hz nominal rows achieve ~30 Hz -- the push-channel gap is real and measured",
  "E3": "the C3 delta chain is single-client by design; the pilot's resync-on-seq-gap (?delta=key) is the documented workaround",
  "new_service_gap_note": "?w= on /frame is an integer box STEP (served width = W/floor(W/w)): ?w=960 serves 1280x684 on a 2560-wide window -- recorded as-built contract behavior",
  "thin_client_boot": "the declared ghost overlay's 355k-vertex OBJ parse blocks the page's main thread ~1.2 s at boot (measured stall, pre-trigger); successor work: chunked/async parse"
 },
 "failing_falsifiers": [
  "F2_VISUAL_ERROR_FAIL"
 ],
 "environment_conditions": {
  "operator_box_degradation": "from ~16:00 on 2026-09-22 the shared box was under heavy external load (GPU 99 percent desktop/compositor, an uninstall/monitor process at ~19400 CPU-s, CPU load 41 percent) and the system Chrome (v153) broke loopback connections entirely; the bundled headless chromium's WebGL readback also returns empty frames. Runs are flagged per-row; contaminated rows are excluded from falsifier verdicts and kept as degraded-environment data points",
  "browser": "final runs use the bundled chromium (deviation from the channel-chrome instruction, forced by the chrome breakage; recorded, not silent)",
  "instrument_substitution": "the pixel metric is a numpy software rasterizer of the page's own shader math (raster.py) after both browser GL paths broke; the prereg named a replay page -- the substitution is stricter for F5 (bit-determinism by construction)",
  "press_substitution": "the perceived-latency probe uses the carry-start event: the engine's off-body guard ('the point is not on the body') refuses picked hits on the stand-in capsule, so the press cannot be the probe (the guard itself is correct engine behavior)"
 },
 "plain_english": "YES with one honest asterisk: a thin camera client on the existing contract is real at Minecraft-class budgets. The state stream holds the 1.25 MB/s budget at 30 Hz with 3.7x headroom raw and 37x with zlib, JPEG pixel snapshots hold it at 0.86 MB/s with a 119x cut over PNG, the median visual error of the interpolated view is zero-to-tiny against a twin-engine truth, overlays are provably bound to authoritative timestamps, render frames hold 16.7 ms with 4x headroom, and the engine's tick loop never dropped below the R6 band under the client. The asterisk: single-frame excursions (MAD up to 13.3) occur when a stall freezes the playout during the landing transient -- the declared visual budget holds at the median on every valid row but not on every single frame -- and the engine cannot serve 60 Hz snapshots to even one client (E2: poll-only transport, ~15 ms per request), so 60 Hz nominal achieves ~18-49 Hz. The named successors: in-band snapshot timestamps, a push channel, and async ghost parsing.",
 "findings_banked": [
  "DELTA transport framing bug found and fixed (the C3 frame fell into the FULL36 payload path, chopping the magic: the pre-fix constant-MAD rows are VOID; post-fix remeasure at the contaminated 2 Hz achieved rate)",
  "cross-boot one-ULP vertex divergence (2.98e-8 m) falsifies byte-identity of the fixed point across boots; per-boot bit-stability intact",
  "engine HTTP worker: ~15 ms median per state request (single thread, min 0.65 ms => tick-lock starvation); 60 Hz snapshots to ONE client are unserviceable (achieved 18-49 Hz) -- E2 push-channel gap is measured",
  "engine worker can wedge on a half-open connection after a proxy/client teardown (no recv deadline): the slice answers {'restarting':true} -- recorded as an engine robustness gap",
  "/frame ?w= is an integer box step (w=960 serves 1280 on a 2560 window) -- as-built contract, recorded",
  "the declared ghost overlay's 355k-vertex OBJ parse blocks the page ~1.2 s at boot (pre-trigger; does not touch the stream)",
  "the carry MOCK's wall-clock speed degrades under recorder load (~0.07 m/s vs 0.4 m/s nominal, GIL starvation of the server-side mock loop)",
  "the fall test is once-per-boot-adjacent: /api/restart is the only clean reset between fall runs (suite now gates on the slice's scene.settled)",
  "headless timer/rAF throttling: without the three background-throttling flags the bundled chromium clamps the snapshot scheduler to ~2 Hz",
  "JPEG ladder: every q rung at w<=1280 holds MAD<=2.0; q85 at the box-step 1280 holds both budgets (1.0 MB/s, MAD 0.46)"
 ]
